# Keep Git LFS intentionally minimal and avoid tracking local engine binaries or deployment artifacts.
# The public repo is source-first; secrets, engine archives, and local runtime state stay outside Git.
# If a binary truly needs versioning later, add a specific pattern intentionally and deliberately.

# Default: no global LFS tracking for this public repo.

# Linguist hints remain conservative so source code is still the primary language signal.
*.py linguist-language=Python
*.yaml linguist-language=YAML
*.yml linguist-language=YAML
*.md linguist-documentation
*.txt linguist-documentation
*.pgn linguist-documentation
*.csv linguist-documentation
*.json linguist-documentation
* linguist-vendored
*.py linguist-vendored=false
